# The reprobuild-packages catalog. A `uses:` name the stdlib does not bundle is
# looked up in a `reprobuild-packages` checkout beside the consuming project
# (or an ancestor), or beside this checkout -- which is where this entry puts
# it. `sqlite3` moved there, then `shellcheck`, `shfmt` and `prek`, and each
# move is a compile ERROR when no catalog defines the package, so without this
# checkout every recipe this suite compiles that uses one of them stops: runquota's repro.nim
# (t_b0_runquota_repro_nim_compiles), CodeTracer's (the `ct` build), and
# t_uses_resolves_sqlite3_from_real_
# reprobuild_packages, which exists to prove the real catalog -- not the
# fixture under tests/reprobuild-packages -- defines what consumers rely on.
# t_import_of_a_moved_stdlib_module_names_the_new_home compiles `uses:` of all
# three lint tools against the real catalog, so the pin must be a revision
# that defines them (they arrived in eed38ec). t_e2e_home_profile_reaches_
# catalog_apps resolves a home profile's `ghostty` and `iterm2` from the real
# catalog and asserts their records, which arrived in 9f981af.
#
# Cloned at the revision repro.lock records, so the catalog content the suite
# asserts against does not move under a commit; the release archive ships that
# same revision (scripts/release/stage_release_catalog.sh). It is not a flake
# input: no Nix-sandboxed build here compiles a recipe, and
# $REPROBUILD_PACKAGES_ROOT in the dev shell would replace the fixture catalog
# the lookup test walks to.
reprobuild-packages


